From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shaders/colorspace: the NLQ of the Dolby Vision decoding on
 the resampled layer, not rounded

Since 684894fc, sh_dovi_compose_nlq() takes the enhancement layer in its
own codes (the offset, slope and threshold of the RPU as they are, the
residual bounded by hdr_in_max, the colour clamped to [0, 1]) and rounds
the value it is given to an integer before the LINEAR_DZ dequantization,
as clause 5.4 of ETSI GS CCM 001 applies it to integer EL codes.

Where the layer is scaled to the picture, though, the value at an output
sample is an interpolation of the layer's codes by libplacebo's scaler,
not a code of the layer. The clause scales the layer's codes with the
integer filters of its informative annex B, which libplacebo does not
reproduce, so rounding the interpolation does not give the clause's
code: it moves the residual by a whole step of the slope wherever the
interpolation is near the middle of two codes, and it turns the float
differences between two renders of the same frame into whole steps. With
a bilinear scaler for the layer (libplacebo-9920), many samples fall
exactly on that middle.

The value is now used as it is. What 684894fc brought stays: the units,
the (|rr| - 0.5) form, the bound by hdr_in_max and the clamp. A value
within float noise of the offset (2^-22 of the larger of the two, the
guard that this series had before 684894fc) is taken as the offset, so
that a layer at its offset adds no residual, as with the rounding.
Nothing else changes; the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 (libplacebo-9930)
does not use this function.

Measured on Mesa's zink with three pictures of a 3840x2160 profile 7 FEL
stream, the transport converted to BT.2020 YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits, against
a reference made with the composer of the clause and an exact Lanczos
stage after it, over the active area, in 12-bit codes: the picture decoded
from the transport has 56.7 % of its pixels a code or more off (mean
0.818) instead of 61.0 % (0.872), its luma 22.1 % instead of 33.4 % and
its chroma 23.2 % instead of 17.9 %. With the layer scaled bilinearly, the
two renders of a frame that a player makes (into a picture that it then
packs, and packed as it is drawn) differ in 0.3 % of their chroma codes,
by 1, instead of 5.5 %, by up to 2.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the file changed,
whose notice stays as it is.
---
 src/shaders/colorspace.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shaders/colorspace.c b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
index d14a58bd..80e96393 100644
--- a/src/shaders/colorspace.c
+++ b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
@@ -138,13 +138,20 @@ void sh_dovi_compose_nlq(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_dovi_metadata *data,
         .data = hdr_max,
     });
 
-    // LINEAR_DZ dequantization of the EL codes, rounded to integers after
-    // the resampling: rr = 0 gives no residual, otherwise
+    // LINEAR_DZ dequantization of the EL codes: rr = 0 gives no residual,
+    // otherwise
     //   residual = sign(rr) * ((|rr| - 0.5) * slope + threshold)
-    // bounded by hdr_in_max
+    // bounded by hdr_in_max. rr is the value of the EL as it is given, not
+    // rounded: where the EL is scaled, it is an interpolation of its codes
+    // and not a code of it, and rounding it moves the residual by a whole
+    // step of the slope wherever it is near the middle of two codes. A value
+    // within float noise of the offset is taken as the offset.
 #pragma GLSL /* sh_dovi_compose_nlq */                                  \
     {                                                                   \
-    vec3 rr = round($el_signal().rgb - $off);                           \
+    vec3 el_sample = $el_signal().rgb;                                  \
+    vec3 rr = el_sample - $off;                                         \
+    vec3 noise = 2.384185791015625e-7 * max(abs(el_sample), abs($off)); \
+    rr = mix(rr, vec3(0.0), lessThanEqual(abs(rr), noise));             \
     vec3 res = sign(rr) * ((abs(rr) - 0.5) * $slp + $thr);              \
     color.rgb += clamp(res, -$mx, $mx);                                 \
     color.rgb = clamp(color.rgb, 0.0, 1.0);                             \
